topic: Provider-supported pre-inference skill visibility controls for Claude Code and Codex

questions[6]{id,question,trace_targets}:
  RQ-001,Does Claude Code expose a supported control point that can prevent irrelevant skill content before it enters model context?,GAP-001/DEP-001/RISK-001
  RQ-002,Does Codex expose a supported control point that can prevent irrelevant skill content before it enters model context?,GAP-001/DEP-001/RISK-001
  RQ-003,What can Context Guard control without modifying authoritative skill bodies or introducing its own compact skill index?,GAP-001/GAP-002/DEC-004
  RQ-004,Which installed client versions and diagnostic surfaces can verify visibility before a paid model inference?,GAP-001/GAP-004/RISK-001
  RQ-005,Which Claude Code surfaces can apply per-skill visibility before session-start context is built while preserving explicit invocation?,GAP-001/DEC-009/BR-206/BR-208
  RQ-006,Which Codex configuration layers and client surfaces actually affect the model-visible skill list before thread start?,GAP-001/DEC-009/BR-206/BR-208

sources[12]{id,title,locator,type,accessed_at,credibility,notes}:
  SRC-001,Extend Claude with skills,https://code.claude.com/docs/en/slash-commands,official-documentation,2026-07-27,Primary Claude Code product documentation.,Documents progressive loading;  invocation controls;  listing behavior;  and the full-skill lifecycle.
  SRC-002,Claude Code hooks reference,https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks,official-documentation,2026-07-27,Primary Claude Code hook contract.,Documents Skill PreToolUse;  UserPromptExpansion;  InstructionsLoaded;  and their timing.
  SRC-003,Codex skill-creator reference implementation,https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/skills/src/assets/samples/skill-creator/SKILL.md,official-source-code,2026-07-27,OpenAI-owned Codex repository and bundled skill guidance.,Defines intended Codex progressive disclosure for metadata;  skill bodies;  and resources.
  SRC-004,Codex app-server protocol documentation,https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/app-server/README.md,official-source-code,2026-07-27,OpenAI-owned current app-server protocol documentation.,Documents skills/list;  skills/config/write user-level configuration;  explicit skill injection;  thread startup;  and usage events.
  SRC-005,Current Context Guard provider adapters,context_guard/adapters/claude_code.py and context_guard/adapters/codex.py,internal-source-code,2026-07-27,Direct inspection of the repository implementation under refinement.,Read with events.py;  engine.py;  and cli.py to establish the existing lifecycle/tool boundary.
  SRC-006,Context Guard product-goal discovery evidence,specs-refiniment/003-context-guard-product-goal/discovery.md,internal-evidence,2026-07-27,Sanitized observations from local Claude Code and Codex session logs.,Shows pre-work cache-token activity but does not attribute it solely to skill content.
  SRC-007,Anthropic prompt caching,https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching,official-documentation,2026-07-27,Primary Anthropic API usage-field contract.,Defines cache creation;  cache read;  and uncached input token semantics.
  SRC-008,Claude Code settings,https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings,official-documentation,2026-07-27,Primary Claude Code settings contract.,Documents skillOverrides values;  settings-local persistence;  plugin limitation;  and the v2.1.129 minimum.
  SRC-009,Codex project-local skill filtering limitation,https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/20210,vendor-issue,2026-07-27,OpenAI repository issue with a reproducible current configuration-layer limitation; corroborated locally.,Reports that project-local skills.config entries do not affect the model-visible list while user/global configuration does.
  SRC-010,Version-pinned local client diagnostics,Local commands: claude --version/--help; codex --version/--help; codex debug prompt-input,local-diagnostic,2026-07-27,Direct execution against the installed clients without a model inference.,Claude Code 2.1.218 exposes settings;  setting-source;  full-skill-disable;  print;  and IDE flags. Codex CLI 0.144.1 exposes command-line configuration;  app-server;  and model-visible prompt rendering.
  SRC-011,Disposable Codex skill-visibility capability fixture,Ephemeral nested repository executed locally and removed after sanitized counts were captured,local-test-evidence,2026-07-27,Controlled no-inference A/B test against Codex CLI 0.144.1.,Baseline listed the probe skill once; project-local skills.config still listed it once; explicit command-line skills.config listed it zero times. Separate tests showed selected global entries and skills.include_instructions affect prompt construction.
  SRC-012,Sanitized local provider usage samples,Local Claude project JSONL and Codex rollout JSONL under the user home directory,internal-observation,2026-07-27,Direct schema and counter inspection without retaining prompts;  source content;  credentials;  or raw responses.,Supports the provider-specific measurement adapter contract in DEC-011.

findings[18]{id,statement,source_ids,confidence,limitations,trace_targets}:
  RF-001,In a regular Claude Code session;  skill descriptions are placed in context while full bodies load only when invoked; irrelevant full skill bodies are not normally a startup-context cost.,SRC-001,high,Preloaded subagent skills are an exception and behavior is version-dependent.,GAP-001/DEP-001
  RF-002,Claude Code has supported controls that reduce skill-listing context without rewriting a skill body: disable-model-invocation in owned frontmatter and skillOverrides in settings.,SRC-001/SRC-008,high,skillOverrides does not apply to plugin skills; frontmatter changes are not an acceptable generated intervention for authoritative third-party skills.,GAP-001/GAP-002
  RF-003,Claude hooks that observe or block a Skill call run after the model-visible skill listing is assembled and therefore are not a generic initial-context rewrite boundary.,SRC-001/SRC-002,high,This is an inference from documented hook timing and scope.,GAP-001/DEP-001/RISK-001
  RF-004,Codex uses progressive disclosure: name and description metadata are the routing surface and full SKILL.md content loads after explicit selection or trigger.,SRC-003/SRC-004,high,End-to-end token traces remain necessary to quantify contribution.,GAP-001/DEP-001
  RF-005,Codex app-server supports skills/list plus user-level enable or disable by absolute path or name;  and explicit skill input injects the authoritative full instructions.,SRC-004,high,The configuration write mutates user-level state and must be paired with rollback; app-server behavior may not map to every client version.,GAP-001/GAP-002/BR-208
  RF-006,The current Context Guard implementation is not skill-aware and cannot presently manage provider skill visibility or profile skill loading.,SRC-005,high,Reflects the current working tree only.,GAP-001/GAP-002/DEC-008
  RF-007,Observed pre-work cache-token activity proves a measurement problem but not that full skill bodies caused it; both providers normally expose metadata before invocation rather than every body.,SRC-001/SRC-003/SRC-006,high,Controlled contribution isolation has not yet run.,GAP-001/GAP-004/RISK-001
  RF-008,GAP-001 is feasible only through provider-specific startup configuration;  not a generic runtime hook.,SRC-001/SRC-002/SRC-003/SRC-004/SRC-005,high,Supported client surfaces and configuration-layer constraints must remain explicit.,GAP-001/GAP-002/DEC-008
  RF-009,Claude cache usage for DEC-003 is the sum of cache creation and cache read tokens across unique responses in the declared window;  with local transcript deduplication by request and message identity.,SRC-007/SRC-012,high,Claude Code transcript schema must be version-preflighted.,GAP-004/DEC-003/DEC-011
  RF-010,Codex measurement should prefer exact per-completion cached input; a validated local rollout fallback uses cumulative total deltas and never sums re-emitted last-token snapshots.,SRC-004/SRC-012,medium,Exact raw completion events are experimental and rollout schemas may drift.,GAP-004/DEC-003/DEC-011
  RF-011,The provider pilot requires paired fresh sessions;  standardized cache priming;  alternating order;  hard quality gates before measurement;  and no statistical outlier deletion.,SRC-007/SRC-004/SRC-012,medium,Pilot defaults require dry-run validation.,GAP-004/DEC-010/DEC-011
  RF-012,The installed clients are Claude Code 2.1.218 and Codex CLI 0.144.1; both are new enough to expose the documented or diagnostic configuration surfaces used by this capability matrix.,SRC-008/SRC-010,high,The matrix must be rerun whenever either client version changes.,GAP-001/GAP-004/RISK-005
  RF-013,Claude Code 2.1.218 can apply per-skill visibility from settings before its session skill listing is built. user-invocable-only is the conservative irrelevant-skill action because it removes model visibility while preserving explicit user invocation; name-only is a lower-savings fallback and on preserves normal behavior.,SRC-001/SRC-008/SRC-010,high,No no-inference prompt renderer exists in the inspected CLI;  so the exact local listing delta still requires the first controlled Claude pilot; plugin skills are excluded.,GAP-001/DEC-009/BR-206/BR-208
  RF-014,Claude CLI interactive;  print;  and IDE-connected sessions share startup settings surfaces;  but generated profiles must be passed before session creation; hooks or mid-session settings changes cannot earn startup savings for the active session.,SRC-001/SRC-002/SRC-008/SRC-010,medium,IDE parity is inferred from the shared Claude Code process and --ide surface rather than a separate IDE-specific skill visibility contract.,GAP-001/BR-208/RISK-001
  RF-015,Codex CLI 0.144.1 applies explicit startup skills.config overrides before model prompt construction. In no-inference diagnostics;  disabling each absolute-path duplicate removed one inventory entry and disabling both removed both; a global include-instructions switch removed the complete skills section.,SRC-010/SRC-011,high,The global switch is too coarse for DEC-009 and is not the recommended MVP action.,GAP-001/DEC-009/BR-208
  RF-016,Codex CLI 0.144.1 did not honor a repository-local .codex/config.toml skills.config entry for the disposable probe skill;  while the equivalent command-line startup override removed it from the model-visible prompt.,SRC-009/SRC-011,high,This result is version-pinned and may change; repository-local filtering must remain capability-tested rather than assumed.,GAP-001/RISK-001/RISK-005
  RF-017,Codex app-server and app-server-backed clients have a supported user-level configuration path through skills/config/write and can verify state with skills/list; changes must happen before thread/start and be rolled back after the run.,SRC-004,high,The local app-server mutation flow was not executed because it would alter user-level configuration; IDE and desktop client versions still require preflight.,GAP-001/BR-108/BR-208
  RF-018,GAP-001 is definition-complete for a bounded MVP: support Claude non-plugin skills through startup skillOverrides and Codex CLI/app-server sessions through generated startup or user-level profiles; require a new session;  actual-state verification;  rollback;  and full-load fallback. Repository-local Codex filtering;  Claude plugin skills;  unsupported IDE versions;  and mid-session interception are not supported optimization surfaces.,SRC-001/SRC-004/SRC-008/SRC-009/SRC-010/SRC-011,high,Execution qualification still requires a controlled Claude listing/token run and Codex app-server/IDE preflight; unsupported surfaces remain measurement-only/full-load.,GAP-001/DEC-009/DEC-011/RISK-001

open_questions[3]{id,question,owner,next_action}:
  OQ-001,Do the installed Codex IDE and desktop clients use the same pre-thread user-level skill state as Codex app-server 0.144.1?,Engineering,Run skills/list before thread/start in each installed client surface and compare the enabled inventory digest without sending a model turn.
  OQ-002,How many provider-reported cache tokens are attributable to skill metadata versus other startup instructions?,Product and Engineering,Execute the DEC-011 controlled baseline and guarded pilots after the adapters and runner exist.
  OQ-003,Should Claude plugin skills and Codex repository-local configuration become a later compatibility slice?,Product,Keep them out of the bounded MVP unless pilot demand justifies a provider-specific follow-up capability.
